{"assets":["/statement-assets/93605d85dc72a6bce55e187c0587f5fa33c02928b26aeecb06c65a5dfbb9989d.png","/statement-assets/b3f2f2ad5f04b8d8ce85c83cde460ae1049beea65a0d0b63bce138ff57c274ba.png","/statement-assets/e69c3ed0afe4e7416701c1d4a248db74cf2c6cb63b88b9078b6cc4b1057f220e.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1001","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Distinguish multi-qubit basis states"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" qubits which are guaranteed to be in one of two basis states on "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"N"},{"kind":"text","text":" qubits. You are also given two bitstrings "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits0"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits1"},{"kind":"text","text":" which describe these basis states."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to perform necessary operations and measurements to figure out which state it was and to return 0 if it was the state described with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits0"},{"kind":"text","text":" or 1 if it was the state described with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits1"},{"kind":"text","text":". The state of the qubits after the operations does not matter."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to implement an operation which takes the following inputs:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" an array of qubits "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"qs"},{"kind":"text","text":","}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" two arrays of boolean values "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits0"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits1"},{"kind":"text","text":", representing the basis states in which the qubits can be. These arrays will have the same length as the array of qubits. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits0"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"bits1"},{"kind":"text","text":" will differ in at least one position."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"An array of boolean values represents a basis state as follows: the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th element of the array is true if the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th qubit is in state "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/93605d85dc72a6bce55e187c0587f5fa33c02928b26aeecb06c65a5dfbb9989d.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":", and false if it is in state "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/b3f2f2ad5f04b8d8ce85c83cde460ae1049beea65a0d0b63bce138ff57c274ba.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, array [true; false] describes 2-qubit state "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/e69c3ed0afe4e7416701c1d4a248db74cf2c6cb63b88b9078b6cc4b1057f220e.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your code should have the following signature:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"namespace Solution {\n    open Microsoft.Quantum.Primitive;\n    open Microsoft.Quantum.Canon;\n\n    operation Solve (qs : Qubit[], bits0 : Bool[], bits1 : Bool[]) : Int\n    {\n        body\n        {\n            // your code here\n        }\n    }\n}"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1001F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1001/problem/F"}